<Legal title="Privacy Policy" updated="September 3, 2026">
  <p>
    SessionSeal seals a musician's master, stems, and session file into a
    signed, timestamped record. This policy explains, in plain language, what
    we collect to do that, what we do with it, and what we never do with it.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account details.</strong> When you sign in with Google we
      receive your name, email address, and profile picture. We don't see
      your password, and we ask for no other Google data.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The files you seal.</strong> Your master, stems, and session
      file, stored privately so your record can be verified later.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Evidence derived from those files.</strong> Watermark payloads,
      acoustic fingerprints, cryptographic hashes, and the results of our
      coherence checks.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Verification requests.</strong> When anyone asks us to check a
      copy, we log the request — including the uploaded file's details, the
      result, the requester's IP address, and browser information — as an
      audit trail.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cookies.</strong> One session cookie to keep you signed in.
      No advertising trackers, no analytics cookies from third parties.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is public by design</h2>
  <p>
    A sealed record exists to be checked by others. For each record we
    publish a signed manifest containing the artist name you provide, the
    record's identifier, timestamps, and the verification summary. Treat the
    artist name field as public. Your audio files themselves are
    <strong>not</strong> public.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>
    To create and verify records, keep your account working, investigate
    abuse, and improve the service. That's the whole list. We do not sell
    your data, we do not use your music to train anything, and we do not
    share it with advertisers.
  </p>

  <h2>Where it lives</h2>
  <p>
    Files and records are stored with Amazon Web Services in the Asia
    Pacific (Mumbai) region, encrypted in transit. Sign-in is handled by
    Google. These providers process data on our behalf and on their own
    terms.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Records are the product — a proof that vanishes is no proof — so sealed
    records and their evidence are kept until you ask us to delete them.
    Verification logs are kept as an audit trail. If you delete your
    account, we delete your files and records; note that manifests already
    published may have been copied by others while public.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:raj@sessionseal.com">raj@sessionseal.com</a> to
    see, export, or delete your data. We'll act on it and tell you when it's
    done.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>SessionSeal is not directed at children under 13.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes in a way that matters, we'll note it here with a
    new date. Continued use after a change means you accept it.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    SessionSeal · <a href="mailto:raj@sessionseal.com">raj@sessionseal.com</a>
  </p>
</Legal>
